"text": "[image: Protecting Our Environment illustration] Protecting Our Environment Lydia is committed to protecting the Great Lakes which hold 20% of the world's surface freshwater. Securing vital federal funding for water infrastructure. She will preserve Michigan’s iconic landscapes Read More",
"href": "https://www.lydialynnchristensen.com/issues/protecting-our-environment"
},
{
"text": "[image: Protecting the Great Lakes and Upper Peninsula Waters from Mining Pollution illustration] Protecting the Great Lakes and Upper Peninsula Waters from Mining Pollution Mining operations threaten Michigan's watersheds and the Great Lakes. Lydia will oppose permits that allow mining discharge into waters that flow toward Lake Superior, push for federal enforcement of the Clean Water Act with real teeth, and put the burden of proof on the polluter instead of on fish and communities. Read More",
"href": "https://www.lydialynnchristensen.com/issues/protecting-the-great-lakes-and-upper-peninsula-waters-from-mining-pollution"
},
{
"text": "[image: Unchaining Michigan’s Clean Energy illustration] Unchaining Michigan’s Clean Energy Equal tax treatment for every energy source, a fix for the federal permitting queue stalling wind and solar, an end to Michigan's cap on electric choice, faster nuclear licensing without cutting safety, and transparency in energy research so breakthroughs reach the public instead of getting shelved. Read More",
"href": "https://www.lydialynnchristensen.com/issues/unchaining-michigan-s-clean-energy"
